From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: cv18xx: select the mux parent on bypass mux reparent

bypass_mux_set_parent() only toggled the "bypass" bit: selecting a real
parent (index > 0) cleared the bypass but left the underlying mux field
at its previous value. On the SG2000 EVB this defeated
assigned-clock-parents for CLK_CAM0_200: the DTS asks for disppll, the
bypass bit is cleared, but the mux still points at the 25 MHz crystal.

The UARTs inherit clk_cam0_200, so base_baud stayed at 1,562,500 and
stty 2000000 failed (EINVAL) - no SLIP link at the modem 2 Mbaud.

Write the mux field as well (index - 1, matching get_parent +1 offset).
Muxes that never reparent are unaffected: with index 0 the bypass bit is
still set and the mux field is not used.

--- a/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-ip.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv18xx-ip.c
@@ -592,7 +592,8 @@
 	if (index == 0)
 		return cv1800_clk_setbit(&mux->mux.common, &mux->bypass);
 
-	return cv1800_clk_clearbit(&mux->mux.common, &mux->bypass);
+	cv1800_clk_clearbit(&mux->mux.common, &mux->bypass);
+	return mux_set_parent(hw, index - 1);
 }
 
 const struct clk_ops cv1800_clk_bypass_mux_ops = {
